+
+## Request
+
+Review how `applyPatch` checks and applies patches and make it conform to RFC 6902, errors included.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+- A `value` of `add`, `replace` or `test` that is not a JSON value (NaN, Infinity, undefined, holes,
+  non-plain objects, cycles) makes the patch invalid and throws.
+- A sparse patch array (holes) is not silently skipped: the hole is an invalid operation and throws.
+- All other RFC 6902 behaviour (appendix A, atomic failure, move/copy/test rules) is unchanged and tested.
